CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: integration-only
SCALE_REALISM: L0 demonstrates the toy mechanism, but scale realism is insufficient: pure-Python Aho-Corasick, planted spans, no real tokenizer/SSE runtime, no real vLLM/SGLang/TGI stream, no real deployed moderator. More importantly, NeMo already ships the systems design knob pair (chunk_size + context_size) and explicitly documents boundary-spanning context for output rails, so the claimed W/chunk seam is already operationalized in a shipping guardrails system.
RATIONALE: Prompt version v001. The core mechanism is not just prior academic intuition; NVIDIA NeMo Guardrails documents output-rail streaming under rails.output.streaming with chunk_size/context_size/stream_first, says chunk_size is the number of tokens buffered before output rails run, context_size helps decisions across chunk boundaries, and context overlap retains last context_size tokens and prepends them to next chunk’s processing context. The code implements this via RollingBuffer. vLLM and SGLang confirm realistic runtime stream_interval knobs, but the claimed safety coupling is already addressed by NeMo’s shipped output-rail streaming design. The packet’s L0 is reproducible as a harness-level artifact, but as systems contribution it is mainly rediscovering/benchmarking a known chunk-plus-context integration pattern rather than a new systems insight.
